y, \"local_id\") reads'","AC4: 'A regression test pins no local/Jira duplicate growth for the perturbation above.'","Harness described as 'real git + real ticket CLI + the stateful Jira fake' — no statement that the fake stores/returns entity properties"],"finding":"AC4 verifies the fix via the stateful Jira fake, but the plan does not confirm that fake implements Jira entity-property get/set (get_issue_property / the local_id property). If the fake does not support entity properties, the new property-read signal path is never exercised and the test passes without proving the changed behavior.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3490ad58bfc7b311","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC4 / 'Exact perturbation' section ('the stateful Jira fake')","norm_id":"n837725c79fc0e267","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Fake returns None/empty for get_issue_property, so suppression never triggers, yet duplicates also don't appear in the fake for unrelated reasons — test green, prod path unproven"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to AC4: assert the fake round-trips get_issue_property, and assert the outbound/inbound arms took the re-confirm/stand-down branch (e.g. a log/counter) rather than only asserting final entity counts.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ensure AC4 exercises the real `get_issue_property` suppression against a fake that faithfully stores/returns Jira entity properties (or document the fidelity), and add coverage for the property-absent branch (AC3) so suppression fires only when the property is genuinely present.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0611,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Perturbation harness uses 'the stateful Jira fake; no production Jira or store'","AC2 introduces new behavior keyed on get_issue_property, but AC4 only says 'pins no local/Jira duplicate growth for the perturbation above'","No AC asserts the fake stores/returns entity properties as live Jira does, nor a test for the property-absent branch that AC3 hands to the keyless-pending grace"],"finding":"AC4's regression test runs against 'the stateful Jira fake', and the new suppression depends on `get_issue_property` returning the `local_id` property. The plan does not state that the fake faithfully models Jira entity-property storage/retrieval; if the fake auto-returns or ignores properties, the test would pass without exercising the real property-read suppression path (proxy-validation risk). The plan also does not test the property-absent (crash-before-write, AC3) branch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe7b5fe96c4081306","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC4 / 'the stateful Jira fake'","norm_id":"nebc0e26d31b417e3","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend AC4: (1) assert the fake persists and returns the local_id entity property set on create; (2) add a case where the property is absent and confirm the keyless-pending grace/recovery path owns it rather than the new suppression.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify error handling for the new per-issue get_issue_property reads: on read failure fall back to the existing label+binding guards (fail-safe, no create), and surface the failure via a log/metric rather than aborting the pass.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4475,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'enrich each fetched Jira snapshot entry by direct per-issue get_issue_property(issue_key, \"local_id\") reads'","No mention of what happens if get_issue_property errors/times out for one issue in the working set","Reconciler already performs writes and external Jira calls (adds a failure point per the T5b overlay trigger)"],"finding":"AC2 adds a per-issue get_issue_property read for every working-set Jira issue on every pass, a new external failure point, but the plan states no error handling, timeout, or blast-radius behavior when that per-issue read fails or is slow.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4cd4f36ad5354afd","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2","norm_id":"n88510c74ec6c4d19","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Jira slow/erroring on one issue's property read mid-pass","A property-read exception aborting the whole reconcile pass instead of degrading to prior guard behavior"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that a failed property read is treated as 'property unknown' → defer create (fail closed) and emit a warning/metric so the degraded state is observable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define 'active local ticket' in AC2 (e.g. the local id resolves to a ticket that still exists in the store / is not closed-deleted), so the suppression predicate is unambiguous.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'use that property to suppress inbound adopt/snapshot-differ creates and outbound creates when it points at an active local ticket'","No definition of 'active' (exists? not closed? not deleted?) given"],"finding":"AC2 says to suppress creates 'when it points at an active local ticket' but does not define 'active'. Whether a closed/deleted/tombstoned local ticket still counts is left to the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2e2afff7661d5f11","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2","norm_id":"n505e16f4008d025b","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The referenced local ticket was legitimately deleted/closed — should suppression still fire, or should a create proceed?"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure disposition of the per-issue `local_id` property read: whether a read failure is transient/retryable (skip enrichment for that issue, disposition falls back to the existing two guards) or fatal, so a failed enrichment cannot silently reintroduce the duplicate.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'enrich each fetched Jira snapshot entry by direct per-issue get_issue_property(issue_key, \"local_id\") reads'","No disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal) is stated for a failed per-issue property read","This adds an external-dependency failure arm the reconciler did not previously depend on"],"finding":"AC2 adds per-issue `get_issue_property(issue_key, \"local_id\")` reads during snapshot fetch — a new external Jira call per working-set issue — but the plan states no failure disposition for that read. If a property read fails/times out for an issue, the plan does not say whether the pass fails fatally, skips that issue, or degrades to the prior two-guard behavior.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5b1ae8a8aee8dd5b","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2 / Implementation decision ('directly read that key's local_id entity property and attach it to the snapshot')","norm_id":"nd322b313809d0621","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a line: a failed property read is treated as 'property absent' (transient/degrade to existing guards) rather than aborting the pass, so enrichment failure never blocks reconcile and never silently re-enables duplication.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State AC2's disposition when the per-issue local_id property read fails (transport error / KeyError / not-yet-indexed): specify whether the create is deferred (fail-closed, aligning with the keyless-pending grace) or proceeds (fail-open), and justify the choice against the duplicate risk.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'enrich each fetched Jira snapshot entry by direct per-issue get_issue_property(issue_key, \"local_id\") reads'","fetcher.py:557 'fail-open per project' and access_check.py:219 shows get_issue_property can raise KeyError on a malformed response","ABSENCE: the plan states no read-failure behavior, yet whether the third signal fails open (duplicate returns) or closed (create deferred) is load-bearing for whether the fix holds"],"finding":"AC2 mandates a per-issue get_issue_property read to enrich each snapshot entry but does not specify the failure disposition of that read (transport fault, KeyError/malformed response, or DC index lag on the property itself). The surrounding fetcher enrichment fails open per project (fetcher.py:557-577); if the property read is likewise treated fail-open (property absent), the outbound create and adopt arms fire and the +1/+1 duplicate returns for that pass, silently defeating the fix under exactly the transient-fault conditions duplicates are most likely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6ef68030a81585bb","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria / AC2; Implementation decision","norm_id":"n165eed6514048572","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Property read raises a transient transport error during a pass where the binding+label are already lost","The local_id property is subject to its own index/read lag on DC"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend AC4 (or add an AC) to also pin zero-growth/zero-write for perturbations a (label intact, binding gone) and b (binding intact, label gone) after the third signal is added.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC4: 'no local/Jira duplicate growth for the perturbation above' (perturbation d only)","Plan measures perturbation a: 'zero growth, zero Jira writes' and b: 'total no-op' as current behavior","No AC re-pins a/b behavior after adding the third signal"],"finding":"AC4 pins convergence only for perturbation d (both guards gone), but the plan's own 'Why the existing guards do not prevent it' section relies on perturbations a and b remaining no-ops. Adding the third signal could regress those; no criterion pins that a-only and b-only still produce zero growth after the change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffad75d35bb15abfd","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC4 vs 'Why the existing guards do not prevent it'","norm_id":"n4ba9c8cc8dd27736","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["New suppression interacts with the label/binding guards and changes the a-only or b-only path"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Define AC2's behavior when the enriched local_id property does NOT resolve to an active local ticket (deleted/archived/foreign id): confirm the create/adopt proceeds (mirroring _adopt_stands_down's resolve-from-local-state check) rather than being blanket-suppressed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5487,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'suppress ... creates when it points at an active local ticket'","binding_walk.py:394-408 shows the existing adopt guard treats a foreign/ambiguous or non-resolving marker distinctly rather than blanket-standing-down","ABSENCE: the plan defines only the 'active local ticket' case, not the stale-pointer / foreign-id case"],"finding":"AC2 says to suppress creates when the property 'points at an active local ticket' but does not define behavior when the fetched issue's local_id property points at a local ticket that no longer exists (deleted/archived) or at a foreign/ambiguous id. Without that carve-out the suppression rule is under-specified at exactly the boundary where the binding-walk adopt arm already draws careful distinctions (see _adopt_stands_down's marker/ambiguity checks at binding_walk.py:394-401).","group_criteria"